# Scheduly Frontend UI, Forms, And Quality

- Build screens with primitives in `src/components/ui` before adding new ones. Merge classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`. Icons from `lucide-react`.
- Tailwind only; tokens via CSS variables in `src/index.css` (`.dark` theme).
- User-facing copy is Spanish (Uruguay). Keep labels, toasts, loading, empty, and error states consistent.
- Compound components only where subparts share state (`Dialog.Root`, `Tabs.Trigger`, `ClassFilters.StudentField`). Simple one-offs take explicit props.
- Login uses React Hook Form + Zod. Existing student/subject/class forms may stay custom until migrated. Do not claim RHF on every form.
- Every data-driven view handles loading, empty, and error. Destructive actions use `AlertDialog`.
- Accessible controls: labels, button `type`, keyboard-friendly behavior.
- Phone layout is the default; `lg` is enhancement. See `scheduly-frontend-mobile-first.mdc`.
- Before finishing substantive UI changes, run `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test`, and `npm run build`, and verify the flow in the browser.

## Scheduly-specific chrome

- Paid status: green = pagada, orange/destructive = pendiente, yellow = gratis — keep toggles prominent.
- Discount badges: violet when `discountPercent > 0`.
- Forms: `Dialog` + `Label` + `Input` + `Select` + `Switch`. Show API errors in Spanish.
- Class form: ≥1 subject and ≥1 attendee; subject price multiples of $50 UYU.
- Student form: ≥1 contact with non-empty `value`; contacts are `{ id, type, value }[]`.
- Do not hardcode login credentials in the UI.

## Calendar

- `react-big-calendar` + `date-fns` localizer, `es` locale, week starts Monday.
- Calendar CSS in `src/index.css` via `.rbc-*`. Do not restyle from a feature file.
